One Application, Four Clouds
A global Kubernetes architecture
21 Oct 2026
Tags: kubernetes, architecture, multicloud, Cloudflare, Workers

Rael Garcia
@raelga
https://github.com/raelga/kubernetes-talks

* What we want to achieve

- Run the same application across four cloud providers.
- Route users to a regional deployment through one hostname.
- Keep application data accessible from every region.

* The approach

.image images/overview/configuration.svg _ 900

* The target architecture

.image images/overview/global-picture.svg _ 900

* Cloudflare Workers: logic at the edge

.image images/overview/workers.svg _ 900

* From a user to a regional application

.image images/overview/request-path.svg _ 900

HTTPS terminates at Cloudflare; origin connections use HTTP in this implementation.

* Shared data across regions

.image images/overview/shared-datastore.svg _ 900

D1 is a shared external database, not a database replicated between the clusters.

* Architecture boundaries

- Four independent clusters, not one stretched Kubernetes cluster.
- Geographic routing, not measured lowest-latency routing.
- Regional application deployments still depend on Cloudflare and shared D1.

